WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:03.789
This is the executive
briefing for Book 18 of the

3
00:00:03.789 --> 00:00:07.725
Federal Modernization Workbook,
Application Modernization.

4
00:00:07.725 --> 00:00:12.213
It's for the people who make the
calls: the CIO, the chief architect,

5
00:00:12.213 --> 00:00:18.225
portfolio owners, the CISO, the privacy
officer, authorizing officials and sponsors.

6
00:00:18.225 --> 00:00:19.675
The argument is simple.

7
00:00:19.675 --> 00:00:24.300
An agency with thousands of legacy
applications can't rewrite its way out.

8
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:28.918
It decides, one application at a time,
what each one becomes, and builds the

9
00:00:28.918 --> 00:00:33.612
ones that change on one architecture,
with the data proven and the AI owned.

10
00:00:33.612 --> 00:00:36.849
I'll take four questions:
why, what, who and how.

11
00:00:36.849 --> 00:00:41.225
Each decision slide names the decision,
its owner and when it's needed.

12
00:00:41.225 --> 00:00:43.250
Let's start with where the money goes.
